### Page 13 of 15

```text
We will use the TIPS training to train all of our employees to safely serve alcohol. We plan to retain all
team member and any new team member will be trained within 90 days. Below is additional information
about the TIPS program.
The TIPS program is an internationally recognized alcohol education program that deals with many areas
of alcohol awareness; from retail programs, to college students, to adult consumers. The primary class
taught by the WSLA is the On-Premise program, a four to five hour class teaching graduates to:
•
Help stop drunk driving and other alcohol related problems before they occur.
•
Allow liquor retailers, law enforcement, elected officials, and citizens to work together to solve
common problems.
•
Effectively curb underage purchases and use of alcohol and tobacco.
•
Train liquor retailers, bartenders and servers how to deal with problem situations
•
Give liquor retailers a thorough understanding of Wyoming law
•
Enhance profits, reduce expenses, and make better tips while improving customer service
```

